MLpot test case: ammonia in water
=================================

test_mlpot_asparagus.py exercises the MLpot module end to end: it builds the
system, evaluates the energy first with CGenFF and then with a trained
machine-learning model potential, and continues with a structure optimization
and short heating and NVE runs so that energy conservation can be checked.

There are two MLpot tests, and they cover different things:

  test_mlpot_energy_terms.py    the MLPO/MLEL energy-term plumbing, driven
                                with stub callbacks.  Needs nothing
                                installed and runs in the normal sweep.

  test_mlpot_asparagus.py       this one.  Needs ASE, Asparagus and the
                                trained model, and runs real dynamics.


Running it
----------

1. Install CHARMM/pyCHARMM as instructed.

2. Install Asparagus, which supplies the model potential:

     git clone https://github.com/MMunibas/Asparagus.git
     cd Asparagus
     python -m pip install .

   and put it on PYTHONPATH:

     export PYTHONPATH=/home/user/Asparagus:$PYTHONPATH

3. It is marked `slow`, so the default sweep skips it.  Ask for it by name:

     cd tool/pycharmm
     pytest -m slow tests/test_mlpot_asparagus.py

   It also still runs on its own, the way the original script did:

     python tests/test_mlpot_asparagus.py

Without ASE, Asparagus or the model present it skips rather than failing,
which is what happens on a machine that has none of them.


The model
---------

data/model_nh3/ holds the trained model this test uses: config.json and
best/best_model.pt.  The configuration ships with "device": "cpu" so the test
runs on a machine without a GPU.  Change it to "cuda" to use one.
